lost his mind.

00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:46.171
Where were you when it happened?
- I was at NBC watching it at the time—

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.298
- Going nuts.
- Going nuts, yelling

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:49.924
cuz he kept going—

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:52.427
- Tony Dungy's like,
"Wow. Wow. Wow."

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:54.054
But we talked—

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.514
I looked in the camera last week
and said, "You're crazy

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:59.392
if you don't think the playoffs
are goin' through New England."
- Right.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.394
- Then that happened—
- Yeah.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.354
- And now you're crazy if the playoffs
aren't going through Kansas City.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:05.774
- Right, right.
- They had that two-game lead.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.859
That felt like
a huge shift in power.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.028
Is that gonna change
the entire playoffs?

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:12.572
- I think it definitely increases
the chance of the Chiefs

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.324
getting to the Super Bowl
in the AFC.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:16.493
I think that's what it does
more than anything.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.620
I mean, one thing we've seen
with New England

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.498
if there's a flaw, and
there's not many flaws
with New England

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:24.292
they haven't won a road playoff
game since 2006.

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:27.504
Now, granted, they've played
some good teams on the road

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.380
whether that was
Peyton Manning's Colts

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.508
or those Denver Bronco defenses—
- Yeah.

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:34.844
- And dealing with that
in the Mile High Stadium.

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:38.139
But the big thing is, you get
New England outta New England.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:40.225
New England's like
the old Yankee Stadium.

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:41.810
When you walk in there,
you're like

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.771
"The ghosts of Belichick
and Brady are haunting me"

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.689
and, "Can we overcome
this crowd?"

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:48.942
And because they understand
how good their team is

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.819
the crowd stays quiet,
and Brady can make

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.445
nine million checks
at the line of scrimmage.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.905
That goes by the wayside—
- And they put, like

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:55.532
audio recording stuff
in your locker room.

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:57.367
- Well, now, you're saying that.
- And they cut off

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:58.910
your communication
in the third quarter.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.328
- You're such
a conspiracy theorist.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.831
- I love that Belichick and Brady
have ghosts

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.958
and they're still alive.
That's how good they are.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.209
- That's how good they are.

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:08.461
- What's up? It's Baker Mayfield.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.713
You're watching "Simms &amp; Lefkoe"
on Bleacher Report.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:13.967
- So we wanna put
our guest to work.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.804
Champ Bailey. Top-three,
top-five corner all time?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.348
- Damn. I think he's
in the top-five discussion.

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:22.517
I mean, I'm not just gonna go
out crazy and say top three.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.852
- Hall of Famer?
- Hall of Famer.

00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:25.395
- Hall of Famer. Get him in, get him in.
- Hands down.

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:27.564
- Come on, guys.
You can exaggerate a little.

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:28.982
- Only DB I ever
practiced against

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.859
that actually scared me
in practice.

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:33.069
- There's a lotta good wide
receivers in the league right now.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:36.156
I wanna know
how you'd cover them.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.449
First one: Tyreek Hill.

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:40.034
So, you're Tyreek Hill.
Step to the line.

00:02:40.034 --> 00:02:42.036
- Oh, you know me.
I'm Tyreek Hill, all right.

00:02:42.036 --> 00:02:43.288
- You're Tyreek Hill? OK.

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:44.789
- Yeah. You still
gonna get up there?

00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:46.416
- Really?
- Absolutely.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:48.793
I mean, we're both fast.
I mean, we're both fast.

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:52.088
I won't do this every play,
but I gotta get in your face.

00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:53.673
I gotta let you know I'm here.
- Right.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.800
- I mean, that's my bread
and butter, bump-and-run.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.510
Now, I'm not stupid.
- Right.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.262
- This boy runs a 4.2,
maybe a 4.1

00:02:59.262 --> 00:02:59.846
- This boy runs a 4.2,
maybe a 4.1

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.265
so I'm aware of that
before I play him.

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:04.726
So my idea of playing him
from the line of scrimmage

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.436
is I gotta stay
in front of him.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:08.771
You hear this old cliche:
"Get your hands on him."

00:03:08.771 --> 00:03:11.399
Man, forget that. It's not about
gettin' your hands on him.

00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:13.109
It's about stayin'
in front of him

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:14.861
makin' it hard
for him to get there.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.529
That's the easy one.
That's the one they want.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.238
That's the easy one.
That's the one they want.

00:03:17.238 --> 00:03:18.823
- And you're not gonna try
to jam him?

00:03:18.823 --> 00:03:20.033
- Of course I'm gonna try
to jam him.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.325
- OK, I thought
you weren't sure.

00:03:20.325 --> 00:03:20.992
- OK, I thought
you weren't sure.

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:23.161
- No, the hands are secondary.
- I think you're crazy, Champ.

00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.288
- The hands are secondary.
So I gotta stay on top of him.

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:27.749
If he wants to run
a 15-yard comeback, curl,
you can have that.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.667
I'mma come down.
I'mma pound you all day.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:30.210
I'mma come down.
I'mma pound you all day.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.378
- All right. I'm going time out–
- Right.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.256
- Because I believe you've seen the film.
- Yeah.

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:38.176
- I think a lot of corners have thought
that with Tyreek Hill this year.

00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:38.218
- I think a lot of corners have thought
that with Tyreek Hill this year.
- Yeah.
- And that first–

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.219
- Yeah.
- And that first–

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:39.260
- Yeah.
- And that first–
- We're talking about me though, right?

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:40.511
- We're talking about me though, right?

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.764
- I know I'm talking about you.
- Set him straight!

00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:44.265
- I know this–
- Just want to be clear.

00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:50.480
but if he did open up on you and
it looked even faster than it was on film.

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:55.068
Are you coming out earlier? I'm just saying,
like, I haven't seen anyone in the NFL–

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:59.530
