first play and I'm chasing.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.005
I'm like, "Oh my god, this guy's faster than I thought."
- Yeah.

00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:18.675
- I played off him a little more than I wanted to but–
- Okay.

00:04:18.716 --> 00:04:22.095
- At the same time, I still got up in
his face when I had the chance.

00:04:22.136 --> 00:04:24.514
You know, it's just being aware
of what the situations are.

00:04:24.555 --> 00:04:26.349
There's a lot of layers to it, man.
- Yes.

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:27.725
I could go on and on about–

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:28.393
- Let's do another one: Antonio Brown.
- OK.

00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:29.769
- Let's do another one: Antonio Brown.
- OK.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.479
- There's part of me
that believes

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:34.899
that if you saw Antonio Brown,
it's lockup status.

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:36.109
that if you saw Antonio Brown,
it's lockup status.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:38.861
It's "I gotta get my hands on him
big-time." Super-physical.

00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:40.154
Am I right?
- You're right.

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:41.823
I'mma tell you
why you're right.

00:04:41.823 --> 00:04:43.408
Because film study tells me—

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.702
this is what I know because
I've played against him

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:47.662
I've seen him
throughout the years.

00:04:47.662 --> 00:04:49.580
He has a hard time
with big, long corners.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.416
- Right.
- Richard Sherman gives him hell.

00:04:51.416 --> 00:04:52.583
- Hell.
- Hell.

00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:54.252
- So I'm aware of that.

00:04:54.252 --> 00:04:55.753
- And no one factors this into
the best wide receiver—
- Jalen Ramsey is givin' him hell.

00:04:55.753 --> 00:04:57.922
- Give him hell, you know?
It's hard for him.

00:04:57.922 --> 00:04:59.590
And why is it hard for him?

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.259
Because they stay in front
of him, they make it hard.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:02.510
He can't run around him

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.304
he can't just wiggle
and just go.

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:06.347
The tape will tell you
everything. Tape doesn't lie.

00:05:06.347 --> 00:05:06.973
- I agree.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:10.393
- What about goin' toe-to-toe
with a Julio for that long?

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:12.061
Like, is that
physically demanding?

00:05:12.061 --> 00:05:14.397
Like, are you exhausted more
after that game

00:05:14.397 --> 00:05:16.482
than after a game
against Antonio Brown?

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.526
- You know, a guy like that,
he's bigger

00:05:18.526 --> 00:05:20.570
so he's not gonna have
the same release

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.698
but he's stronger, so your feet
really play a role there

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:25.408
because if you're just standing
there with your arms out like this—

00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:27.660
- Oh, you're getting tossed.
- He's just, you know, a la Brandon Marshall.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.703
- Oh, you're getting tossed.
- He's just, you know, a la Brandon Marshall.

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:30.663
- Or he's gonna give
you the jerk-through.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.415
- I mean, yeah.
These guys grab you.

00:05:32.415 --> 00:05:33.791
They want you to grab 'em.

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:34.000
They want you to grab 'em.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.960
But I'll try to get
my hands on 'em

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.171
but it's really more
about my positioning.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:40.965
You know, I just wanna make sure
that I have a strong foundation

00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:43.968
because they'll throw you by,
they'll grab your helmet.

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.846
I mean, it doesn't matter.
Fitzgerald, he's the king of that.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.639
He'll grab you, pull you.
- Right.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:50.641
- And another thing you have to
worry about is blocking.

00:05:50.641 --> 00:05:52.810
Those dudes block
their asses off.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:56.230
- Of all the guys right now,
whether it's Odell, Julio

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.776
Keenan Allen, Antonio Brown,
DeAndre Hopkins, Tyreek Hill

00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:03.071
which one are you goin'
"60 minutes—

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:05.198
I could get anything,
I could get everything

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.909
that's gonna cause me
to earn my paycheck the most?"

00:06:07.909 --> 00:06:11.204
- Well, I think, uh, Odell
is probably the scariest

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:14.248
because his run after the catch
is superb.

00:06:14.248 --> 00:06:15.917
I mean, his first step
is superb.

00:06:15.917 --> 00:06:16.042
I mean, his first step
is superb.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.086
There's really not a lot
of weaknesses in his game.

00:06:18.086 --> 00:06:19.295
- Yeah.
- He can catch everything.

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:20.004
- Yeah.
- He can catch everything.

00:06:20.004 --> 00:06:21.672
You know, his route
running is excellent.

00:06:21.672 --> 00:06:23.049
- We've been saying this
for years.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.092
- Oh, yeah?
- But people haven't believed us.

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:25.343
- Oh, yeah?
- But people haven't believed us.

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:26.928
- Yeah, well, people
wanna hate on Odell.

00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:29.138
- I get it. I mean,
he's a little flamboyant.

00:06:29.138 --> 00:06:31.474
You know, he likes
the limelight, like to dance.

00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:33.768
You know, so what?
- But he's still awesome.
- What does he do between the lines?

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:35.812
- Right, right.
- That's all that matters, right?

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:38.022
So, you know, that's why
people love to hate on T.O.

00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:39.899
but T.O.'s one of the best ever.
- Yeah.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.944
- And, you know, just, you know,
just watching his game

00:06:42.944 --> 00:06:45.363
there's really not a lot
of weaknesses, plain and simple.

00:06:45.363 --> 00:06:47.156
- Yeah.

00:06:47.156 --> 00:06:50.576
- I love the fact that we got to
see how you play the guys.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.788
The other aspect of defending
a wide receiver

00:06:53.788 --> 00:06:55.623
the quarterback eyes.
- Mmhmm.

00:06:55.623 --> 00:06:57.792
- We've had a few
secondary guys here—

00:06:57.792 --> 00:06:59.627
Landon Collins,
Jamal Adams—

00:06:59.627 --> 00:07:03.589
that kind of shared that staring
contest with the quarterback

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.425
and you're tryin'
to figure it out.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:07.677
Is there one that pops
to your head right away

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:10.304
of, whether it's a Peyton
or a Brady or somebody

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:12.640
that game where
they either got you

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.852
or you got them really good?

00:07:15.852 --> 00:07:18.855
- You know, uh,
Philip Rivers, probably.

00:07:18.855 --> 00:07:21.941
One of those guys—he always
let you know when he got you.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:24.152
You know, I hated him
for about two years.

00:07:24.152 --> 00:07:26.070
- [Laughing]
- Great guy. Love him to death.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.322
But he was just hard
to deal with

00:07:28.322 --> 00:07:30.658
you know, because he would—

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:33.536
You could tell
he studied your weaknesses

00:07:33.536 --> 00:07:36.414
because, you know,
he would find those moments

00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:38.166
when you just weren't
paying attention.

00:07:38.166 --> 00:07:40.293
And he knew he couldn't
attack me the whole game

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:42.837
but he had his moments where
he would just throw it in there

00:07:42.837 --> 00:07:45.590
squeeze it in there,
and the guy was accurate.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.508
The ball looks like
it's floating, but it's not.

00:07:47.508 --> 00:07:49.844
- I feel like he would say
something, too.

00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.138
- He would, yeah.
"Yeah, I got you right there."

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:55.099
Or, you know,
he'd come back and—

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:56.350
"You jumped that one.
Don't do that again."

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.518
"You jumped that one.
Don't do that again."

00:07:57.518 --> 00:07:59.353
Or something crazy like that.

00:07:59.353 --> 00:08:02.064
It's, like, half the time
I don't know what he's saying

00:08:02.064 --> 00:08:04.442
but I know he's just
talking trash and just—

00:08:04.442 --> 00:08:06.777
You know, he's a competitive dude.
- Yeah.

00:08:06.777 --> 00:08:09.363
- And I appreciate it more now
than I did then.

00:08:09.363 --> 00:08:12.116
- You played with
Deion Sanders in D.C.

00:08:12.116 --> 00:08:14.202
What was that year like
with him?

00:08:14.202 --> 00:08:16.245
Like, what'd you learn from him,
just bein' around him?

00:08:16.245 --> 00:08:18.122
- You know, it's not just him.
It was Darrell Green, too.
- Oh, man.

00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:20.458
- So, I had Darrell Green
my rookie year—

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:22.251
- Holy cow.
- That's unbelievable.
- And then Deion comes in

00:08:22.251 --> 00:08:23.961
and I got, OK,
two Hall of Famers.

